{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird","id":1046337,"title":"Is Solar on Solar, sexual or romantic relationships, weird?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-09T08:52:46-08:00","id":1046337,"title":"Is Solar on Solar, sexual or romantic relationships, weird?","content":"How would you deal with sexual or romantic relationships between Solars of a single circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:56:35-08:00","id":1046340,"title":"","content":"It's not any weirder, at its heart, than anything else. Solar/Lunar pairs aren't universally romantic (or even friendly) and if Solars acquire a case of the doki-doki for each other, such is things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:02:53-08:00","id":1046343,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't think there's anything weird or out of place for it at all. The older books placed a very heavy emphasis on the Solar-Lunar bond, but that's definitely played down in this edition. And as Beans said, it's never a romantic requirement or enforcement. Love is love and it can happen anywhere. I actually really favor players that end up with romantic relationships with normal mortals. It's very humanizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:19:01-08:00","id":1046370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046343#post1046343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Love is love and it can happen anywhere. I actually really favor players that end up with romantic relationships with normal mortals. It's very humanizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would not be able to enter into a romantic relationship of a deeper nature with someone I know would live but a fraction of my life span. Which is why the characters I run are more likely to seek a relationship with another immortal.<br /> <br /> On a further note, what kind of complications would you see between a returning solar and one of the other types of exalted?<br /> <br /> &quot;Clair we all know that you are dating an abyssal just to piss your father off for being to hard on you. But come on he is outside of fate and brings death where ever he goes. Though its not like last months Dawn caste solar was much better on the massive death front.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:50:00-08:00","id":1046379,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't see why it could be an issue as long as all of the players are comfortable with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:56:58-08:00","id":1046381,"title":"","content":"Complications are between half and three quarters of the fun---so long as no OOC issue arises, you just get lots of interesting things to play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:02:29-08:00","id":1046383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046370#post1046370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would not be able to enter into a romantic relationship of a deeper nature with someone I know would live but a fraction of my life span. Which is why the characters I run are more likely to seek a relationship with another immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god that is a bleak point of view. Fortunately I don't think the themes of <i>Exalted </i>support it in the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:05:07-08:00","id":1046384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046370#post1046370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally would not be able to enter into a romantic relationship of a deeper nature with someone I know would live but a fraction of my life span. Which is why the characters I run are more likely to seek a relationship with another immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wLoh_hfR4o8\" data-code=\"wLoh_hfR4o8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wLoh_hfR4o8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:10:28-08:00","id":1046385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046383#post1046383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good god that is a bleak point of view. Fortunately I don't think the themes of <i>Exalted </i>support it in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an issue that comes up in real life (sans the &quot;immortal&quot; part) when falling in love with someone who is significantly older or who suffers from a terminal illness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:46:33-08:00","id":1046395,"title":"","content":"Oh I know. But people still <i>do </i>that, don't they? They don't just decide &quot;Oh I'm not going to love this person because it won't last <i>forever</i>.&quot; After all, Ayesha Ura's decision to do something similar has been previously cited as an example of exceptionally alienating and abnormal behavior.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the body of myth-narratives that form the foundations of <i>Exalted </i>is that mortal endeavors are not portrayed as pointless simply because people die, and relationships are not to be avoided just because they will eventually end. I recently lost a beloved pet. He had been my constant companion for about twelve years. It was absolutely devastating. Yet, I knew when I adopted him that I would outlive him. That, and the knowledge that his eventual passage would be painful, didn't stop me from loving him as much as I did. I still feel broken, yes, but what I wanted was <i>more </i>time with him, not less. I wouldn't go back and avoid the pain by avoiding the love that makes it hurt so keenly now.<br /> <br /> I know that my wife could be hit by a bus tomorrow. One of us is going to endure the death of the other at some point, it's true, but that won't stop us from loving each other now. That's <i>crazy talk</i>.<br /> <br /> The idea that one should only invest in forever because anything less is pointless strikes me as just as absurd in <i>Exalted </i>as it does in real life. It ignores all the complexities of real human experience in favor of a one-dimensional fear of loss. I can only imagine an Exalted character that adheres to such a philosophy as being the opposite of heroic: an object lesson in futility, tragedy, and nihilism. I suppose you could sketch out a half-decent Abyssal antagonist from that, but only for the sake of roundly defeating him and consigning his loathsome philosophy to the ash-heap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:50:58-08:00","id":1046400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046395#post1046395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I know. But people still <i>do </i>that, don't they? They don't just decide &quot;Oh I'm not going to love this person because it won't last <i>forever</i>.&quot; After all, Ayesha Ura's decision to do something similar has been previously cited as an example of exceptionally alienating and abnormal behavior.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the body of myth-narratives that form the foundations of <i>Exalted </i>is that mortal endeavors are not portrayed as pointless simply because people die, and relationships are not to be avoided just because they will eventually end. I recently lost a beloved pet. He had been my constant companion for about twelve years. It was absolutely devastating. Yet, I knew when I adopted him that I would outlive him. That, and the knowledge that his eventual passage would be painful, didn't stop me from loving him as much as I did. I still feel broken, yes, but what I wanted was <i>more </i>time with him, not less. I wouldn't go back and avoid the pain by avoiding the love that makes it hurt so keenly now.<br /> <br /> I know that my wife could be hit by a bus tomorrow. One of us is going to endure the death of the other at some point, it's true, but that won't stop us from loving each other now. That's <i>crazy talk</i>.<br /> <br /> The idea that one should only invest in forever because anything less is pointless strikes me as just as absurd in <i>Exalted </i>as it does in real life. It ignores all the complexities of real human experience in favor of a one-dimensional fear of loss. I can only imagine an Exalted character that adheres to such a philosophy as being the opposite of heroic: an object lesson in futility, tragedy, and nihilism. I suppose you could sketch out a half-decent Abyssal antagonist from that, but only for the sake of roundly defeating him and consigning his loathsome philosophy to the ash-heap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to give this post all the likes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:11:08-08:00","id":1046410,"title":"","content":"As far as Solars romancing eachother being weird I can't see a reason for it to be that way unless something about the situation makes it weird. Just them being the same exalt type wouldn't do anything, this isn't werewolf where there is some kind of universe enforced problem* that potentially arises from not seeking outside of type for partners.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I think they were called Metis or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:15:58-08:00","id":1046412,"title":"","content":"If you love someone, and they die, I don't think it's uncommon for that to change the way you feel about letting yourself get close to that loss again. I've no direct experience to call on, and it depends on the person, but I think any of us here will have experienced to some degree at least some kind of lost love (or I'm really skewed on what the common human experience is!). It will change the way you feel about being open to the same situation again, and what you allow yourself to feel on conscious and unconscious levels, and it will shape your behaviour. That's human. There's a range of responses to this, but you wouldn't be unchanged and wouldn't go on as before.<br /> <br /> I think particularly for the Exalted, the first person they love will not necessarily be an Exalt (despite how much common ground there can be), and even the first person they live a mortal lifetime with, but I think over mortal lifetimes though, I do believe the general tendency may be naturally tend to gravitate for long term companionship and intimacy to other immortals who they've lived lifetimes with. Caveats about variable people, etc.<br /> <br /> (Plus Rakan Thulio is probably a hero. Of a tragic sort.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:30:03-08:00","id":1046419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046395#post1046395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that one should only invest in forever because anything less is pointless strikes me as just as absurd in <i>Exalted </i>as it does in real life. It ignores all the complexities of real human experience in favor of a one-dimensional fear of loss. I can only imagine an Exalted character that adheres to such a philosophy as being the opposite of heroic: an object lesson in futility, tragedy, and nihilism. I suppose you could sketch out a half-decent Abyssal antagonist from that, but only for the sake of roundly defeating him and consigning his loathsome philosophy to the ash-heap.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree with the principles you're otherwise stating, but would be a bit uncomfortable with so roundly condemning such a thing. Different people have different experiences and tolerances, and I think a lot of them deserve respect and accommodation as much as anything.<br /> <br /> \u200bAscribing anything universal to anybody tends to have its issues, and when it comes to the Exalted in particular I have a preference for incorporating certain diversities. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:44:32-08:00","id":1046426,"title":"","content":"The only weird thing that I think would come up involves four words: Scroll of Swallowed Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:49:09-08:00","id":1046430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird#post1046337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you deal with sexual or romantic relationships between Solars of a single circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>*blinks* is this a lore thing or a ST thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:06:59-08:00","id":1046444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046395#post1046395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I know. But people still <i>do </i>that, don't they? They don't just decide &quot;Oh I'm not going to love this person because it won't last <i>forever</i>.&quot; After all, Ayesha Ura's decision to do something similar has been previously cited as an example of exceptionally alienating and abnormal behavior.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the body of myth-narratives that form the foundations of <i>Exalted </i>is that mortal endeavors are not portrayed as pointless simply because people die, and relationships are not to be avoided just because they will eventually end. I recently lost a beloved pet. He had been my constant companion for about twelve years. It was absolutely devastating. Yet, I knew when I adopted him that I would outlive him. That, and the knowledge that his eventual passage would be painful, didn't stop me from loving him as much as I did. I still feel broken, yes, but what I wanted was <i>more </i>time with him, not less. I wouldn't go back and avoid the pain by avoiding the love that makes it hurt so keenly now.<br /> <br /> I know that my wife could be hit by a bus tomorrow. One of us is going to endure the death of the other at some point, it's true, but that won't stop us from loving each other now. That's <i>crazy talk</i>.<br /> <br /> The idea that one should only invest in forever because anything less is pointless strikes me as just as absurd in <i>Exalted </i>as it does in real life. It ignores all the complexities of real human experience in favor of a one-dimensional fear of loss. I can only imagine an Exalted character that adheres to such a philosophy as being the opposite of heroic: an object lesson in futility, tragedy, and nihilism. I suppose you could sketch out a half-decent Abyssal antagonist from that, but only for the sake of roundly defeating him and consigning his loathsome philosophy to the ash-heap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. To be clear, I was agreeing with your original post, and I agree with all of this as well \u2014 except for the intensity of the last couple of sentences, where I am inclined to Isator's perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:22:00-08:00","id":1046451,"title":"","content":"To be honest, given all the other types of strange romances in Exalted... from bestiality to incest and everything in between... Solar on Solar romances wouldn't be that strange. We have people having romances with demons, spirits, elementals, ghosts, animals, brothers, sisters, fathers, mothers, sons, daughters (and every other familial relationship)... and even with artificial beings (Alchemicals are technically artificial). If none of that is all that strange in the setting... why would two Solars having a relationship be strange?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe level of comfort your table may have with such relationships between players may vary... but generally in Creation, you will find people with all sorts of fetishes and perversions... and while some may be more common than others... there will be something for everyone somewhere in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:25:05-08:00","id":1046453,"title":"","content":"The only game I've run that had romance in the story had 2 relationships form: 1 Solar on Solar pairing, and a Solar on Abyssal (who eventually redeemed into a Solar) pairing. I've actually never had a Solar - Lunar romance in a game before. All S-L bonds were platonic oddly enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:29:09-08:00","id":1046455,"title":"","content":"These are PCs, right? Then just let them get on with it. And remind them to take their Maiden Tea unless you want to deal with PCs having babies.<br /> <br /> Huh... you know, now I think about it, I've seen quite a few romances between Exalts in game, but not between two Solar PCs. Solar PCs and Lunar PCs, Lunar PCs and Lunar PCs, Solar PCs and Solar NPCs, Solar PCs and Lunar NPCs*... but not two Solar PCs. Hmmm... once in my game, the Twilight PC had a kind of thing with an Abyssal NPC, but it didn't last, and she ended up marrying another Abyssal NPC.<br /> <br /> *But the ones between PCs and NPCs don't seem to get very far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:43:41-08:00","id":1046464,"title":"","content":"I have no experience with two PC Solars but Solar on Solar is well established in the canon and I have used it with PC-NPC pairings before. The idea that they can relate on a very similar level is a very interesting play.<br /> <br /> I have actually had alot of experience at my table with debates about lifespan and we even had it be a source of tension between PCs with different philosphies (although it did almost slip into OOC arguments a couple of times, but it was still fun). Although it is worth noting that methods of prolonging life are fairly common in the setting and disparaging anyones view on the matter with extreme distate is hardly a good way to go about such an interesting topic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:53:20-08:00","id":1046466,"title":"","content":"As to the original question, the same as I would attempt for anything; occasionally, but consistently, let them have scenes together to do something or share something. What these are might be different from other relationships, but that could describe any relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:04:06-08:00","id":1046470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046444#post1046444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. To be clear, I was agreeing with your original post, and I agree with all of this as well \u2014 except for the intensity of the last couple of sentences, where I am inclined to Isator's perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure. Just because I feel strongly about this doesn't mean I expect everyone else to agree. I rather expect that many won't. Certainly nobody needs my permission to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:33:41-08:00","id":1046484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046426#post1046426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only weird thing that I think would come up involves four words: Scroll of Swallowed Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the players of the characters... If they are openly freaky then it could get very awkward in the game... Like he uses performance or athletics charms to enhance things... I activate respect commanding attitude &amp; strength increasing exercise so she has to listen to me awkwardly talk dirty with a strait face while i jackhammer like a quarterback on promnight... she activates graceful crane stance for perfect balance to hang from a ceiling fan... &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T22:14:04-08:00","id":1046631,"title":"","content":"Sun-sun couples would be unusual, simply because there are so few solars in the world, but not for any reason beyond that, and most games clear that hurdle by already having multiple solars meet in the first session. After that, it's all just people being people and doing people things, one of which is falling in love, another is deciding to hook up even if not in love.<br /> <br /> Solars are people writ large, and are chosen from all walks of life. If there is something a human has done in history, it's something a solar might do, too. Only more epically, maybe, if they have charms for that.<br /> <br /> This also goes for any exalt in general, though most other splats have more in the way of social expectations thrust upon them by established factions and recent history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T22:48:15-08:00","id":1046644,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to note that, for the past 700+ years, the post exaltation lifespan of a Solar has been most conveniently measured in hours or possibly days. Never in months.<br /> <br /> So, between a Solar outliving a normal person or vice versa, I know which way my money is going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-10-2017, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T03:12:20-08:00","id":1046697,"title":"","content":"Is this a question about Solars or a question about player characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T03:54:53-08:00","id":1046704,"title":"","content":"&quot;is it strange for two heroic figures who work together to have a relationship, whether sexual or romantic?&quot;. This is the core question stripped of distractions -- being a Solar does not make you stop being human at your core. You may be able to lift a yeddim, or convince anyone of your point of view given time, effort, and adequate evidence or leverage, but the heart does what it wills.<br /> <br /> As stated above, the only strangeness to it is that two of a hundred and fifty or so individuals among the millions in Creation should meet and form a bond -- but this is no stranger than Solar/Lunar, Solar/Sidereal, Lunar/Sidereal, political issues and questions of opportunity and loyalty with the latter two aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:15:07-08:00","id":1046722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046697#post1046697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a question about Solars or a question about player characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my first question too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:24:30-08:00","id":1046725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046704#post1046704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;is it strange for two heroic figures who work together to have a relationship, whether sexual or romantic?&quot;. This is the core question stripped of distractions -- being a Solar does not make you stop being human at your core. You may be able to lift a yeddim, or convince anyone of your point of view given time, effort, and adequate evidence or leverage, but the heart does what it wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As stated above, the only strangeness to it is that two of a hundred and fifty or so individuals among the millions in Creation should meet and form a bond -- but this is no stranger than Solar/Lunar, Solar/Sidereal, Lunar/Sidereal, political issues and questions of opportunity and loyalty with the latter two aside. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that once you get past the astronomically small chances of two Solars ever meeting in the first place - which we kinda have to take for granted, as the game stops working at a fundamental level if we're not willing to suspend disbelief here - then having those Solars form some bonds, potentially even romantic ones, is perfectly normal, as people bond with people with whom they interact regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:03:20-08:00","id":1046768,"title":"","content":"As has been abundantly stated, no, it's not strange from an in-setting standpoint that wouldn't also be strange for any other Celestial Exalt pairing. And it'll probably be interesting for the game, as long as it doesn't take all the stage time from the other players and everyone is comfortable with it.<br /> <br /> Characters smooching is fun. Let them rub together and see what happens. And of course, if you're the ST, make sure that you steadily mine that situation for all the complications. All of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:29:20-08:00","id":1046785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046725#post1046725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that once you get past the astronomically small chances of two Solars ever meeting in the first place - which we kinda have to take for granted, as the game stops working at a fundamental level if we're not willing to suspend disbelief here</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think Circles tend to form by chance, I think they tend to form by several Exalted being drawn to the same places by common interests in the significance of the place, including the actions of one or more of the member Exalted. Look at the new signature Circle; at least half of them, and possibly all, are in Jiara because they were drawn by news of Perfect Soul's crusade.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like ascribing the fact that so many early 20th century literati and intellectuals knew each other to chance, and it's just... they hung out in the same places.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T09:35:41-08:00","id":1046818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046383#post1046383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good god that is a bleak point of view. Fortunately I don't think the themes of <i>Exalted </i>support it in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes its bleak but realistic given the setting. Let me give you a little back story. I married my wife about 3 years ago, she is 8 years younger than me. So I expected that she would likely outlive me in the end. After our first year of marriage we discovered that she has a chronic degenerative disease. Most likely she will be crippled in 10 years and dead in 20. In my darker moments I am constantly struck by the realization that soon she will be going. Don't get me wrong, I love and charish my wife to the ends of the earth. I would not trade here for the world but at the same time if I had to choose between two potential relationships, one of which would die in the relative blink of an eye and another in which I can bond with that person over centuries, I would never choose an early lose.<br /> <br /> As far as weather or not Exalted supports such an idea. Yes it do repeatedly Off the top of my head, it has been mentioned that people try and clone loved ones, attempted to place there soul in another container. (living or otherwise.) Attempting to find their reincarnated souls. Provide expensive longevity poxes, charms, spells, etc.<br /> <br /> The other thing you see is a lot of the opposite reaction to the same thing. People have shallow superficial relationships that they can easily control and end before they get hurt. At least attempt such.<br /> <br /> Edit: having read Ferryman's last post. I think the biggest thing that you are ingnoring here is selection bias. If you have a wide selection of possible mates, that range from bad, to ok, to great. I am not talking about falling in love with someone and then finding out they are ill. I know how that goes and I treasure everyday with my mate. What I am talking about is the human nature to choose the &quot;best&quot; possible mate you can. What ever your conditions for great are. I am pretty sure that most of us do not look for an early painful dead. Its also not indicating that the person in question is unable to love they simply choose the person they think they can have the best relationship with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12422,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","user":"zylosan","date":". 02-10-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T09:44:34-08:00","id":1046819,"title":"","content":"In our Circle we currently have....<br /> <br /> My character who is a member of the family of royal advisors. Has always had a thing for his childhood friend, the Princess (Another PC)<br /> <br /> Who is betrothed to a merchant prince of another nation (Another PC) and has met her Lunar Mate reincarnation<br /> <br /> The Merchant Prince seduced an Abyssal we fought using Black Claw style, and we've been sending dreams of him to her through sorcery<br /> The Prince also used an artifact to make an Exigent that he'd been rivaling with to fall in love with him, though the Exigent's idea of love are much more about possessing someone.<br /> <br /> So things are complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T10:46:39-08:00","id":1046841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046785#post1046785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI don't think Circles tend to form by chance, I think they tend to form by several Exalted being drawn to the same places by common interests in the significance of the place, including the actions of one or more of the member Exalted. Look at the new signature Circle; at least half of them, and possibly all, are in Jiara because they were drawn by news of Perfect Soul's crusade.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like ascribing the fact that so many early 20th century literati and intellectuals knew each other to chance, and it's just... they hung out in the same places.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and that point about Jiara not only relates common interests, but also that the common interest might actually be a Solar.<br /> <br /> If you're a Solar, with these strange powers, on the run from the Wyld Hunt, it's fairly natural, if you hear of other Solars, to want to go join them. Safety in numbers, after all.<br /> <br /> In my own game, most of the PCs joined the party because that party actually tracked them down and asked them to join (which was basically the plot of the first session). I can well imagine that would be fairly common, as Solars are often not very good at keeping word of their deeds from leaking out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-10-2017, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:45:03-08:00","id":1046907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1046484#post1046484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the players of the characters... If they are openly freaky then it could get very awkward in the game... Like he uses performance or athletics charms to enhance things... I activate respect commanding attitude &amp; strength increasing exercise so she has to listen to me awkwardly talk dirty with a strait face while i jackhammer like a quarterback on promnight... she activates graceful crane stance for perfect balance to hang from a ceiling fan... &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Flashbacks to <i>The Bronze</i>...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:56:25-08:00","id":1046917,"title":"","content":"Solar-on-Solar isn't any weirder than any general human-on-human, it would be the player-on-player shtick I might find weird.<br /> <br /> If two players wanted their characters to be in a relationship, I would low-key ask not only the rest of the players at the table, but also myself, if I was ok with that. In most cases ..... I might not, honestly. It would depend on how they portrayed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T17:55:27-08:00","id":1048506,"title":"","content":"I can understand the perspective of desiring a life partner who will have the same general life span as myself. That's why we term it life partner. I own a cat, and I love my cat. I wouldn't go for a long-term relationship with something that is going to be dead in fifteen years, though.<br /> <br /> That being said, my experience with love is it doesn't consult my rational side before deciding to kick me in the stomach with its presence.<br /> <br /> The combination of the above sounds like good story-fuel, assuming everyone at the table is on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T17:57:44-08:00","id":1048509,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that Exaltation for Solars at least doesn't in itself change one's long-term life perspective. If you're a twenty-year-old and Exalt, well...you're still twenty years ould. Most people you found attractive before are that still. And you haven't had the joy of watching many people you love get old and die on you yet, save those who were already old when you first met them. So for many young Solar Exalted, the whole &quot;I'm gonna outlive everyone mortal I love&quot; thing is not quite in the equation yet.<br /> <br /> It coming about, as a note, is often the great motivator of epic plots and such too.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T18:30:16-08:00","id":1048520,"title":"","content":"Really, I find the idea of somebody who will live a long time to have to watch lots of people grow old and die slightly overestimates exactly how many people a Solar will even know, yet alone maintain the kind of relationship that lets you personally witness somebody's evident mortality.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the Exalted probably witnesses a very small number of people die, and consistently receives news of people that they knew for three or four years a few decades ago dying as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven for the close relationships, well; people can manage to have long, full lives alongside spouses or parents and then continue to live for several decades after them. People committing to remain together as long as they're <i>mutually</i> alive is nice, but many people can't really know exactly how long they or others are going to live.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough now I've got an image of a person who recognises that they're going to outlive almost anybody that they love for a long time, and instead of resolving to never love anybody mortal, any mortal spouses they have are people that they distance themselves from when mortality starts to become imminent. Not necessarily casting the person aside as giving them a very cushy estate to retire to so that the Exalt can be spared having to personally witness them.<br /> <br /> Still; immortality may not ever be without costs, but it's not exactly the most difficult thing in the world either. If it really bums one so much, find some sorcery (possibly contained within a sorcerer), or invest in some peaches or bargain with the right kind of spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T00:38:44-08:00","id":1048618,"title":"","content":"It's not <i>weird</i>, but I personally can't see two Solars loving each other more than their...work?/Motivation/life path. They always seem so fiercely independent to me- I can't really envision anything more than casual sex or marriages of convenience. Like 'it was fun while it lasted, but now I have to go steal the Empress' throne and he wants to stay in Gem building houses'. And Solars also seem too competitive to share both a workplace <i>and</i> a home. It's not epic love, it's two oxen pulling a cart in different directions.<br /> I don't believe that 'career' should take precedence over love, but Solars especially need to do their own thing. Lunar mates complement Solars instead of threatening them, and few have any ties to specific places. They can be at home (be useful) anywhere, even if their spouse is raiding tombs one night and swimming to Atlantis the next.<br /> It's not that Solars are egoistic, or that one partner should be 'submissive', it's that nurturing long-term relationships requires both participants to sacrifice time and energy- something they can't do if say, the Circle they're in just barely escaped death, or the lab they worked in blew up an hour ago and just <i>seeing</i> their co-workers reminds them of that failure. Solars breed trouble, and I can't be optimistic about a relationship where the spouses could be having two entirely separate crises every day. It's not 'drama that inspires great romantic efforts', it's 'mundane and frustrating trials that few otherwise successful/exhausted Solars would have any patience with'. Solars lost that sort of patience when they took the Second Breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 02-14-2017, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:40:52-08:00","id":1048722,"title":"","content":"We should consider that in the age of Sorrows, most Solars have a REALLY short life span, thanks to Wyld Hunt. In my Exalted game, one of the Dragonblooded players commented to the Solar player<br /> <br /> &quot;Summoning Second Circle Demons? That's Dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Eh, My character is a Solar hiding on the Blessed Isle. He wasn't playing to live to old age anyways.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the odds of a Solar living thousands of years is very small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:42:48-08:00","id":1048723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird#post1046337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you deal with sexual or romantic relationships between Solars of a single circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's called a 'daisy chain,' and the best way to deal with it is to buy lube in bulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:09:16-08:00","id":1048774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1048722#post1048722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should consider that in the age of Sorrows, most Solars have a REALLY short life span, thanks to Wyld Hunt. In my Exalted game, one of the Dragonblooded players commented to the Solar player<br /> <br /> &quot;Summoning Second Circle Demons? That's Dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Eh, My character is a Solar hiding on the Blessed Isle. He wasn't playing to live to old age anyways.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the odds of a Solar living thousands of years is very small.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not overstate the situation, here. Before the Empress' disappearance, the few Solars who were around did get hunted down relatively early. Now that number has increased by essentially two orders of magnitude, while the Wyld Hunt is being slowly sapped of resources. Meanwhile, the formerly rock-solid Bronze Faction that backs the Realm suddenly finds itself with a newly resurgent competitor .<br /> <br /> Solars don't have free reign, but it's safe to say their average life-span is rocketing upward, and they don't need to make it to thousands of years to feel alienated from mortals. Dragon-Blooded look down on mortals and they are lucky if they hit 300.<br /> <br /> Talking down the survivability of post game-start Solars isn't good for the game. We aren't playing Paranoia, here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:06:12-08:00","id":1048805,"title":"","content":"Although with the Dragon Blooded, at least part of that is due to their social conditioning in service of political and ideological goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:12:15-08:00","id":1048809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1048774#post1048774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's not overstate the situation, here. Before the Empress' disappearance, the few Solars who were around did get hunted down relatively early. Now that number has increased by essentially two orders of magnitude, while the Wyld Hunt is being slowly sapped of resources. Meanwhile, the formerly rock-solid Bronze Faction that backs the Realm suddenly finds itself with a newly resurgent competitor .<br /> <br /> Solars don't have free reign, but it's safe to say their average life-span is rocketing upward, and they don't need to make it to thousands of years to feel alienated from mortals. Dragon-Blooded look down on mortals and they are lucky if they hit 300.<br /> <br /> Talking down the survivability of post game-start Solars isn't good for the game. We aren't playing Paranoia, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify my position here.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that All Solars are Doomed to die because Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying the idea that a Solar has thousands of years to live may not occur to a young Solar. Maybe a Lunar or a Gold Faction Sidereal will enlighten them, but I bet most Solar expect to live a Dragonblooded lifetime at most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:41:49-08:00","id":1048820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1046337-is-solar-on-solar-sexual-or-romantic-relationships-weird?p=1048618#post1048618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not <i>weird</i>, but I personally can't see two Solars loving each other more than their...work?/Motivation/life path. They always seem so fiercely independent to me- I can't really envision anything more than casual sex or marriages of convenience. Like 'it was fun while it lasted, but now I have to go steal the Empress' throne and he wants to stay in Gem building houses'. And Solars also seem too competitive to share both a workplace <i>and</i> a home. It's not epic love, it's two oxen pulling a cart in different directions.<br /> I don't believe that 'career' should take precedence over love, but Solars especially need to do their own thing. Lunar mates complement Solars instead of threatening them, and few have any ties to specific places. They can be at home (be useful) anywhere, even if their spouse is raiding tombs one night and swimming to Atlantis the next.<br /> It's not that Solars are egoistic, or that one partner should be 'submissive', it's that nurturing long-term relationships requires both participants to sacrifice time and energy- something they can't do if say, the Circle they're in just barely escaped death, or the lab they worked in blew up an hour ago and just <i>seeing</i> their co-workers reminds them of that failure. Solars breed trouble, and I can't be optimistic about a relationship where the spouses could be having two entirely separate crises every day. It's not 'drama that inspires great romantic efforts', it's 'mundane and frustrating trials that few otherwise successful/exhausted Solars would have any patience with'. Solars lost that sort of patience when they took the Second Breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know, another side to living for thousands of years is that you get the luxury of having very long periods in which nothing too exciting is happening to you.<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel like you're espousing a perspective on Solars that would make it difficult to conduct any kind of game whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}